Subject: [PATCH] DRM: keep keys pressed and released within one frame

PollKeyboardEvents() set currentKeyState straight from each event, so a
key pressed and released between two frames was up again when the frame
looked at it, and IsKeyPressed(), which compares previousKeyState with
currentKeyState, never reported it. On a slow board, where a frame can
take longer than a short key tap, presses got lost and a key had to be
hit several times.

Keep such a key down until the next poll and release it then.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/platforms/rcore_drm.c | 28 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/platforms/rcore_drm.c b/src/platforms/rcore_drm.c
index 2dcf0fff0..16477fc63 100644
--- a/src/platforms/rcore_drm.c
+++ b/src/platforms/rcore_drm.c
@@ -2376,6 +2376,20 @@ static void ConfigureEvdevDevice(char *device)
 // Poll and process evdev keyboard events
 static void PollKeyboardEvents(void)
 {
+    // PATCH: a key pressed and released within the same frame is kept down
+    // until the next frame, otherwise IsKeyPressed() never sees it. Release
+    // those keys now, after PollInputEvents() has copied the states into
+    // previousKeyState.
+    static bool pendingRelease[MAX_KEYBOARD_KEYS] = { 0 };
+    for (int k = 0; k < MAX_KEYBOARD_KEYS; k++)
+    {
+        if (pendingRelease[k])
+        {
+            CORE.Input.Keyboard.currentKeyState[k] = 0;
+            pendingRelease[k] = false;
+        }
+    }
+
     // PATCH: alle als Tastatur erkannten evdev-Fds pollen, nicht nur
     // den ersten gefundenen (siehe Kommentar bei keyboardFdCount).
     for (int kbdIdx = 0; kbdIdx < platform.keyboardFdCount; kbdIdx++)
@@ -2408,7 +2422,19 @@ static void PollKeyboardEvents(void)
                 // WARNING: https://www.kernel.org/doc/Documentation/input/input.txt
                 // Event interface: 'value' is the value the event carries. Either a relative change for EV_REL,
                 // absolute new value for EV_ABS (joysticks ...), or 0 for EV_KEY for release, 1 for keypress and 2 for autorepeat
-                CORE.Input.Keyboard.currentKeyState[keycode] = (event.value >= 1);
+                if ((event.value == 0) &&
+                    (CORE.Input.Keyboard.previousKeyState[keycode] == 0) &&
+                    (CORE.Input.Keyboard.currentKeyState[keycode] == 1))
+                {
+                    // PATCH: pressed and released within this frame - keep it
+                    // down for this frame, release it on the next poll
+                    pendingRelease[keycode] = true;
+                }
+                else
+                {
+                    CORE.Input.Keyboard.currentKeyState[keycode] = (event.value >= 1);
+                    if (event.value >= 1) pendingRelease[keycode] = false;
+                }
                 CORE.Input.Keyboard.keyRepeatInFrame[keycode] = (event.value == 2);
 
                 // If the key is pressed add it to the queues
-- 
